{
  "schema": 1,
  "description": "Life goals (docs/life-goals.md, supabase/migrations/0021_life_goals.sql). 'timeLeft': how far a by date is from the planning day: whole years when a year or more, else whole months, else days; 'today' on the date and 'past' after it (count 0); null without a by date. Years and months count like birthdays: a month is whole once the day of the month is reached, so January 31 to February 28 is not a month yet. 'order': open life goals by position, then createdAt, then id; then achieved and dropped ones by closedAt, the most recent first, then id. The why reminder: a frequency (daily, every-3-days, weekly) splits time into periods: days, blocks of 3 days from 1970-01-01, or weeks from Monday. A period's number is its index from 1970-01-01 (for weeks, (days since 1970-01-01 + 3) / 7, rounded down). Its seed is the 32-bit FNV-1a hash of the UTF-8 text '<frequency>:<period start>'. The moment is on the period start plus (seed mod length) days, at 10:00 plus ((seed / length, rounded down) mod 600) minutes, then held back by quiet hours like an ordinary reminder (reminders.json). 'whyMoment': the period a day falls in and its moment. 'whyGoal': the open life goal a period shows, the one at (period number mod open count) in their order; null with none open. 'whyDue': at a look, the latest moment after 'since' and up to 'now' among the period now falls in and the two before, or null; 'off' is never due. 'whyNext': the first moment after 'now', for the alarm; null when off. Quiet hours are 'HH:MM-HH:MM' or null. Times are local.",
